<title>SENEGAL: Senegal to liberalise import of oil products.</title>
<headline>Senegal to liberalise import of oil products.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal is to liberalise the importation of oil products in the near future, an energy ministry official said on Tuesday. The Societe Africaine de Raffinage (SAR) currently enjoys a monopoly.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision to liberalise the importation of oil products has been taken. We are just left to implement it,&quot; Alioune Fall, director of energy, told Reuters.</p>
<p>SAR imports 950,000 tonnes of oil products a year, of which 80,000 tonnes are re-exported to neighbouring Mali.</p>
<p>Elf owns 41.8 percent of SAR, Shell 23.6 percent, Total 12.8 percent, Mobil Corp 11.8 percent. The state has a 10 percent stake.</p>
